==============================================================================
  Mutation tests  (assertion-strength validation)
==============================================================================

  Strategy: replace each named fact's body with `{}` (no constraint),
  then re-run Alloy. Each listed assertion should now FAIL on the
  mutated model. If it still PASSes, the assertion is vacuous and
  must be strengthened.

  - MUTATE F_OwnerOrAdminForMutations  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_OwnerOrAdminForMutations.als
    rationale: Removing F_OwnerOrAdminForMutations allows a non-owner MemberRole actor to appear as the actor on a DescChanged or DescDeleted audit entry. Both OwnershipBasedAccess and FR_008_010_OwnerOrAdminCanMutate check exactly that constraint, so they will find a counterexample once the fact is cleared and the violation is injected.
    expected to FAIL: OwnershipBasedAccess, FR_008_010_OwnerOrAdminCanMutate
      - OwnershipBasedAccess: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_008_010_OwnerOrAdminCanMutate: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_CreatedEntryExistsForEveryTask  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_CreatedEntryExistsForEveryTask.als
    rationale: Removing F_CreatedEntryExistsForEveryTask allows a Task to exist with no corresponding DescCreated AuditEntry. AuditCompleteness and FR_015_OneCreatedEntryPerTask both assert 'one ae | DescCreated for every task', which fails immediately. FR_018_AuditRetention fails because 'some ae | ae.aeTask = t' is violated.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_015_OneCreatedEntryPerTask, FR_018_AuditRetention
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_015_OneCreatedEntryPerTask: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_018_AuditRetention: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_DeletedEntryForDeletedTask  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_DeletedEntryForDeletedTask.als
    rationale: Removing F_DeletedEntryForDeletedTask allows a DeletedTask to exist without a DescDeleted audit entry. FR_016_AuditOutlivesTask asserts 'some ae | DescDeleted for every DeletedTask', which fails. AuditCompleteness also relies on this for the deleted-task branch.
    expected to FAIL: AuditCompleteness, FR_016_AuditOutlivesTask
      - AuditCompleteness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_016_AuditOutlivesTask: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_PermissionMatrix  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_PermissionMatrix.als
    rationale: Removing F_PermissionMatrix frees PermMatrix.allowed to take any value. LeastPrivilege checks that MemberRole is not in the PATCH/DELETE cells; injecting exactly that cell violates it. PrivilegeMonotonicity's superset claim and PermissionCompleteness's coverage check also break.
    expected to FAIL: LeastPrivilege, PrivilegeMonotonicity, PermissionCompleteness
      - LeastPrivilege: PASS (vacuous?)
      - PrivilegeMonotonicity: PASS (vacuous?)
      - PermissionCompleteness: PASS (vacuous?)

  - MUTATE F_AuditTeamConsistency  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_AuditTeamConsistency.als
    rationale: Removing F_AuditTeamConsistency allows an AuditEntry to carry a aeTeam that differs from aeTask.taskTeam. NoInformationLeakage, FR_011_014_CrossTeamIsolation, and FR_017_AuditReadableByAnyTeamMember all assert aeTeam = aeTask.taskTeam, so a counterexample is immediately found.
    expected to FAIL: NoInformationLeakage, FR_011_014_CrossTeamIsolation, FR_017_AuditReadableByAnyTeamMember
      - NoInformationLeakage: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_011_014_CrossTeamIsolation: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_017_AuditReadableByAnyTeamMember: FAIL (expected)

  - MUTATE F_CreatedEntryActorIsOwner  → runs/B-L2/mutated_F_CreatedEntryActorIsOwner.als
    rationale: Removing F_CreatedEntryActorIsOwner allows a DescCreated audit entry to be attributed to an actor who is not the task's owner. AttributionCorrectness checks exactly this invariant; FR_006_OwnerImmutable's second clause (created entry actor = owner) also fails.
    expected to FAIL: AttributionCorrectness, FR_006_OwnerImmutable
      - AttributionCorrectness: FAIL (expected)
      - FR_006_OwnerImmutable: FAIL (expected)

